# Infrastructure code. None of it belongs in the application image, and one file
# in here is actively dangerous: terraform/terraform.tfstate holds the generated
# Postgres password in plain text. The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so
# without these lines the state file is uploaded to the registry as part of the
# build context AND baked into a layer, where anyone who can pull the image can
# read it. Excluding it also drops the context from 335 MB to under 1 MB,
# because .terraform/ carries the provider plugins.
terraform/
k8s/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
.terraform/
